==English==

===Alternative forms===
* [[perowne]] {{qualifier|14th-15th centuries}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|xno|en}} and {{etyl|frm|en}} {{term|perron|lang=fro}}, from {{term|pierre||stone}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈpɛɹən/|/ˈpɛɹɒ̃/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{context|historical|lang=en}} A stone block used as the base of a monument, marker etc.
#* '''1485''', Sir Thomas Malory, ''Le Morte Darthur'', Book X:
#*: Now I assygne you to mete me in the medowe by the river of Camelot, where Merlyon sette the '''perowne'''.
# {{context|architecture|lang=en}} A platform outside the raised entrance to a church or large building, or the steps leading to such a platform.

